{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310842,"nonce":"jqPaMK7+1Shuv3qJnxJyY19aRYg=","title":"Temperature + repetition-penalty sampling for llama-chat (commits 70bee09, c2719d2). Greedy Argmax + chat template hit 'in in in in' tail ...","message":"CLI signature: `rayzor run Main.hx -- \u003cmodel.gguf\u003e [prompt] [max_tokens] [ctx] [temperature]`\n\n- **`temperature = 0.0`** → keeps `ArgmaxSampler` (deterministic, greedy).\n- **`temperature \u003e 0.0`** → instantiates the inline `LocalTempSampler(temperature, repetitionPenalty=1.15, seed=42)`.\n\nThe sampler does temperature-scaled softmax + multinomial draw with a sliding-window repetition penalty. Three passes over the logits — maxLogit, softmax denominator, cumulative draw — each applies the penalty consistently via an `adjusted(lg, id, ...)` helper so the denominator matches the values we exp(). No `Array\u003cFloat\u003e` buffer; on-the-fly `Math.exp` keeps memory tiny and dodges the precision-audit edge cases.\n\nRepetition penalty: each call's chosen id goes into a 64-entry ring buffer; subsequent calls reduce the effective logit for any id still in the window (positive logits divided by `penalty`, negative ones multiplied). 1.15 was enough to break the \"in in in in\" tail loops without flattening the distribution; standard chat range is 1.1-1.3.\n\n\nImporting `nue.sampling.TemperatureSampler` from Main.hx triggered a trap-stub cascade — SIGILL in `loop.generate(...)` even when no `TemperatureSampler` instance was ever created. RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS showed valid fn-ptrs for both samplers and BPE methods, no obvious cascade target. Root cause is unclear; the leading hypothesis is the `Array\u003cFloat\u003e` comprehension `[for (_ in 0...n) 0.0]` in `TemperatureSampler.sample` causes a JIT bring-up failure when the class enters compilation.\n\nInlining the sampler in Main.hx without the comprehension fixes the cascade. The original `nue.sampling.TemperatureSampler` is left in place for future use once the import issue is diagnosed.\n\n\nPrompt: `\"What is the capital of France?\"`, Llama 3.2 1B Instruct Q4_K_M.\n\n| Config | Output |\n|---|---|\n| Argmax, raw prompt | `'a country, and the largest country in which is the most …'` |\n| Argmax + chat tmpl | `'Unfortunately, I think the capital of the and the … in in in in in in in of'` |\n| T=0.7 + chat tmpl | `'The current Unfortunately, the capital of Flanders (guessor … in is known to which of some'` |\n| **T=0.7 + chat tmpl + penalty=1.15** | `'The current Unfortunately, the capital of France took place'` — grammatical, no repetition, EOS at 30 tokens |\n\nThe pipeline does its job. Remaining factual weakness (\"took place\" instead of \"is Paris\") is small-model + Q6_K precision drift, not the sampler.\n\n\n- Investigate why `import nue.sampling.TemperatureSampler` triggers the trap-stub cascade. Minimal-repro doesn't reproduce it; only triggers in the full llama-chat pipeline. Fn-ptrs for the imported class are all valid (RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1) so it's not a trap stub — likely a class-layout / vtable issue from class-id renumbering. Inline LocalTempSampler is the working path meanwhile.\n- ~~Streaming display in Main.hx is buggy~~ FIXED in fb84083: wrap `prevLen` / `nTokens` in single-element arrays so closure-by-value capture sees the same heap container. Stream now prints clean per-token deltas; token counter ticks correctly.\n- ~~Real Top-K~~ LANDED in a8ac023: Top-K=50 with insertion-sort scratch (`topKLogits[50]`, `topKIds[50]`). O(n*k) per token vs TopPSampler's O(n²). Repetition penalty applies BEFORE Top-K so recent ids drop out of the candidate pool entirely.\n- Sampler `reset()` would be useful for multi-turn chats so the ring buffer doesn't carry penalties across user messages.\n- Factual coherence — the model still gives weak answers (\"Unfortunately, I don't capital — and live in the\"). Pipeline is correct; gap is precision drift through 16 Q4_K_M layers, not the sampler. Diagnostic recipe (per-layer hidden-state magnitude vs HF reference) queued in [[project-llama-chat-coherence-phase-c]].\n\n\n- [[project-llama-chat-chat-template]] — chat template wrapping. This commit is the sampling complement.\n- [[bugs-array-map-float-audit]] — Array\u003cFloat\u003e precision audit; LocalTempSampler avoids the comprehension on purpose given the audit didn't cover comprehension lowering.\n- [[project-llama-chat-coherence-phase-c]] — bmm + reshape + RoPE that made the model coherent at all.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_llama_chat_temperature_penalty` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}